{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013799R7ArA4YLQDcqkm9d8u","type":"tool_result","content":"760\t/// `Connection`.  Read-only over `connection`; the path may\n761\t/// mutate (the C body updates per-path counters).\n762\tpub trait MemLogHook {\n763\t    fn callback(\n764\t        &mut self,\n765\t        connection: &Connection,\n766\t        path: &mut Path,\n767\t        op_code: i32,\n768\t        current_time: Instant,\n769\t    );\n770\t}\n771\t\n772\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n773\t// QUIC context.\n774\t\n775\t/// Top-level QUIC context.  C: `Quic`.  Single-threaded\n776\t/// scope (per the translation plan): no `Send`/`Sync`.\n777\tpub struct Quic {\n778\t    /// Client-side TLS configuration (set when this `Quic` is\n779\t    /// being used to make outbound connections).  Replaces the C\n780\t    /// `tls_master_ctx` opaque handle for the client role.\n781\t    pub tls_client_config: Option<Box<dyn crate::tls::DynClientConfig>>,\n782\t    /// Server-side TLS configuration (set when this `Quic` is\n783\t    /// being used to accept inbound connections).\n784\t    pub tls_server_config: Option<Box<dyn crate::tls::DynServerConfig>>,\n785\t    /// Application-supplied TLS callbacks (ALPN selection, ticket\n786\t    /// store, certificate verification).  Replaces the C-style\n787\t    /// `register_*` global function-pointer registry.\n788\t    pub tls_callbacks: Option<Box<dyn crate::tls::TlsCallbacks>>,\n789\t    pub default_callback_fn: Option<Box<dyn StreamDataCallback>>,\n790\t    /// Application-supplied state forwarded to the default\n791\t    /// stream-data callback.  Opaque to the library (the C side\n792\t    /// passed it through as `void*`).  Phase 4 may push the state\n793\t    /// into the `StreamDataCallback` impl itself, at which point this\n794\t    /// field disappears.\n795\t    pub default_callback_ctx: Option<Box<dyn Any>>,\n796\t    /// State for the DCID-mask callbacks; opaque to the library.\n797\t    pub mask_ctx: Option<Box<dyn Any>>,\n798\t    pub mask_fns: Option<Box<dyn MaskOps>>,\n799\t    pub default_alpn: Option<String>,\n800\t    pub alpn_select_fn: Option<Box<dyn AlpnSelect>>,\n801\t    pub reset_seed: [u8; RESET_SECRET_SIZE],\n802\t    pub retry_seed: [u8; RETRY_SECRET_SIZE],\n803\t    // C `*mut u64 p_simulated_time` is gone -- the test simulator\n804\t    // owns its own clock and feeds the value through per-call\n805\t    // `current_time: Instant` parameters.\n806\t    /// Application-supplied cryptographically secure RNG.  Replaces\n807\t    /// the C `register_crypto_random_provider` global registry plus\n808\t    /// `Connection::crypto_random` / `crypto_uniform_random` /\n809\t    /// `seed_public_random` accessors.  Used for handshake nonces,\n810\t    /// connection IDs, retry-token integrity nonces, and so on.\n811\t    /// The application installs this at construction time;\n812\t    /// `rand::rngs::OsRng` (wrapped in a `Box`) is the canonical\n813\t    /// default.  Phase 4 may push it down to per-`Connection` if\n814\t    /// per-connection determinism is needed for tests.\n815\t    pub rng: Box<dyn rand::CryptoRng + Send>,\n816\t    pub hash_seed: [u8; 16],\n817\t    pub ticket_file_name: Option<PathBuf>,\n818\t    pub token_file_name: Option<PathBuf>,\n819\t    /// Cached session tickets (replaces the C `p_first_ticket`\n820\t    /// head + per-node `next_ticket` chain).\n821\t    pub stored_tickets: Vec<StoredTicket>,\n822\t    /// Cached retry tokens (replaces the C `p_first_token`\n823\t    /// head + per-node `next_token` chain).\n824\t    pub stored_tokens: Vec<StoredToken>,\n825\t    /// Replay-protection register for new-tokens / retry-tokens.\n826\t    /// Keyed by `token_hash`; values are tokens into the\n827\t    /// per-`Quic` `RegisteredToken` arena.  C: `token_reuse_tree`.\n828\t    pub token_reuse_tree: SplayTree<u64, RegisteredTokenToken>,\n829\t    /// Owning arena